WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
If you're seeing step 5, print pallet labels in your Send to Amazon workflow, this means

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.774
you are sending pallets with an Amazon partnered carrier.

00:00:10.774 --> 00:00:13.240
This step will not show up for any

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.500
other type of shipment.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.280
Now that your pallets are packed and you have confirmed carrier and

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:22.970
pallet information, it is time to print your pallet labels and ship your products.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:23.640
At this

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:30.280
point you should have already placed FBA ID labels on the individual boxes in step 3 and on the

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.030
packed pallets in step 4.

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:35.180
The labels in this step are your carrier labels.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.580
You will need FBA

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:42.032
ID labels and carrier labels on all pallets in order to ship your products.

00:00:42.032 --> 00:00:43.200
Select your pallet

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.946
label type under Print Pallet Labels and Documentation and click Print.

00:00:47.946 --> 00:00:49.240
Place one label

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:54.120
centered and toward the top of each of the four sides of the pallet so that the forklift driver

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.680
can easily see them.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.360
If the pallet contains only one asin, we recommend labeling the pallet

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.740
single asin as well.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:05.880
You're now ready to ship your pallets with your Amazon partnered carrier.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:11.080
To learn about how to manage and track your shipments, as well as create the bill of

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:16.200
lading you will be required to provide your carrier at pickup, please review the Manage your Send

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:16.520
to

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.040
Amazon shipments guide in Seller Central.
